Nega Markel and Prince Harry are taking  legal action against British tabloids on  Tuesday the Duke and Duchess of Sussex  announced that they are suing associated  newspapers the owners of the Daily Mail  Mail Online Metro and more this after  The Mail on Sunday published a private  handwritten letter that Meghan wrote to  her estranged father Thomas Markel in a  statement Harry revealed that this has  been many months in the making  adding quote unfortunately my wife has  become one of the latest victims of a  British tabloid press that we just  campaigns against individuals with no  thought to the consequences a ruthless  campaign that is escalated over the past  year throughout her pregnancy and while  raising our newborn son the 35 year old  new dad goes on to explain that he and  Megan have put on a brave face but he  can't even begin to describe how painful  it has been Harry also calls out the  publications in question for the double  standards that have vilified Megan  almost daily for the past nine months  and says he has been a silent witness to  a private suffering for too long  according to multiple reports the Sussex  is are using private funds for the case  meanwhile ET has reached out to the  Daily Mail and dmg T formerly known as  associated newspapers for more  information we feel a tremendous  responsibility to play our part in  effecting societal change for the better  the issue hits close to home for Harry  his late mother Princess Diana was  hounded by the British press throughout  her life and was fleeing from the  paparazzi when she died in a car crash  in Paris  back in August 1997 the Duke ended his  statement explaining that his deepest  fear is history repeating itself
 

